{\b\fs24 Orchicon}\par
\par
An AI orchestration platform. This package installs the control plane, the command
line, the terminal UI and the desktop app.\par
\par
{\b What this installer puts on this computer}\par
\par
\pard\li240 orchicon.exe\tab the control plane and CLI (install, start, status)\par
orch.exe\tab the terminal UI, a remote client for a plane\par
orchicon-desktop.exe\tab the desktop app\par
\pard\li0\par
It also adds Start menu and desktop shortcuts named "Orchicon".\par
\par
Everything goes under your own user account, in\par
\par
\pard\li240 %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Orchicon\par
\pard\li0\par
so no administrator rights are needed and nothing is written to Program Files. Your
data lives separately, in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\orchicon.\par
\par
{\b What it does NOT contain}\par
\par
The services a plane runs on (PostgreSQL, NATS, the Grafana stack and the
OpenTelemetry collector) are about 540 MB, so they are downloaded during setup
rather than bundled here. Optional runtime container images are downloaded only
if you choose them. Setup needs an internet connection.\par
\par
{\b What happens when you click Finish}\par
\par
A console window opens and runs "orchicon install". It asks three things:\par
\par
\pard\li240 which instance to set up (dev, test or prod)\par
which host ports to use (press ENTER for the defaults)\par
whether to download any runtime images now\par
\pard\li0\par
Press ENTER to accept each default. This step is idempotent and resumable: if it
stops for any reason, run it again and it continues where it left off.\par
\par
\pard\li240 "%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Orchicon\\orchicon.exe" install\par
\pard\li0\par
{\b Requirements}\par
\par
Windows 10 or Windows 11, 64-bit. The desktop app draws its window with Microsoft
Edge WebView2: it is preinstalled on Windows 11, and setup installs it on
Windows 10 if it is missing.\par
\par
{\b Starting and stopping}\par
\par
The desktop app is a client: it connects to a running plane and does NOT start
one. The plane is started by setup, and by "orchicon start" afterwards. If the app
cannot reach a plane it says so and names the address it tried.\par
\par
{\b Uninstall}\par
\par
Use "Apps and features" (or "Add or remove programs"). That removes the binaries
and the shortcuts. Your data directory and any running services are left in
place; to clean those up as well, run:\par
\par
\pard\li240 "%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Orchicon\\orchicon.exe" -Uninstall -Clean\par
\pard\li0\par
